<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<pages:BinderPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:pages="clr-namespace:Foreword.Android.Pages"
             x:Class="Foreword.Android.Pages.RotationsPage"
             Title="Lists">
    <!--
        NOT IN THE APPROVED MOCKUP SET. The mockups draw the prayer document and four app areas; the
        owner's answer at this gate added a second way something gets onto the prayer list — a
        standing list prayed through one a day, "adjustable on the phone app" — and no screen had
        been drawn for it. Built in the grammar of the screens that were: a group label over a
        hairline card, rows that navigate, a pinned bottom bar, and no Save (D35).

        LOADING IS A STATUS SENTENCE, NOT A SPINNER (§6). This screen reads the encrypted archive
        out of Drive, so it has a wait the other settings screens do not, and the sentence says what
        it is waiting for.

        Mockups: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/6bb65b0d-04da-47f3-bf72-a04020217e0c
    -->
    <Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">

        <ScrollView Grid.Row="0">
            <VerticalStackLayout Padding="{StaticResource ScreenPadding}" Spacing="0">


                <Label x:Name="Status" Style="{StaticResource StatusLine}" />

                <Border Style="{StaticResource GroupCard}" x:Name="Card">
                    <VerticalStackLayout x:Name="Rows" />
                </Border>

                <Label Text="One-off requests are written on the journal page, under &quot;Add to the list&quot;. These are the lists that come round again."
                       Style="{StaticResource CardCaption}" />

            </VerticalStackLayout>
        </ScrollView>

        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="1">
            <BoxView HeightRequest="1" Color="{StaticResource Hairline}" />
            <Grid Padding="24,12">
                <Button x:Name="AddButton" Text="Add a list" Clicked="OnAddClicked" />
            </Grid>
        </VerticalStackLayout>
    </Grid>
</pages:BinderPage>
